    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Basra is a traditional fishing game where points are accumulated without a pre-hand wagering requirement.',
      deal: 'The system automated dealer handles the distribution of four cards to players and the floor at the start.',
      reveal_market: 'There is no separate market; cards are played directly to or captured from the central floor tableau.',
      buy_market: 'Players do not buy cards from the table; they capture them through rank matching or numerical summation.',
      buy_stock: 'The deck is distributed in fixed rounds of four cards; players cannot pay to draw extra cards from the stock.',
      fold: 'Players must play all cards in their hand to complete the round; there is no option to abandon the hand early.',
      check: 'The game does not feature a betting structure with checks; every turn requires a card to be played to the floor.',
      call: 'There are no pots or bets to match; progress is measured strictly by point values of captured cards.',
      bet: 'Basra is scored via card accumulation and bonuses rather than through the wagering of chips or currency.',
      raise: 'There are no stakes to increase; the competitive element is focused on maximizing captures and Basra bonuses.',
      declare: 'Results are calculated automatically based on the cards in the score pile; no separate declaration is needed.',
